<article class="env-lemma" id="7FE8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/7FE8">Lemma <span data-tag="7FE8">5.5.9.15</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a category which admits finite products, and ${\mathbf A}\subseteq \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC }$ be the full subcategory spanned by the product preserving functors. For every object $C \in \calC $, the evaluation map ${\mathbf A}\rightarrow \sSet $ preserves homotopy colimits of simplicial objects. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In view of Corollary <a href="/tag/B6B2" data-tag="B6B2">5.5.9.3</a> and Theorem <a href="/tag/B6EE" data-tag="B6EE">4.2.4.1</a>, it will suffice to show that the evaluation functor $\calP _{\Sigma }( \Nerve (\calC )^{op} ) \rightarrow \sSet $ preserves $\Nerve (\cDelta )^{op}$-indexed colimits. This follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/4701" data-tag="4701">5.5.8.10</a>, since $\Nerve (\cDelta )^{op}$ is sifted (Lemma <a href="/tag/61C3" data-tag="61C3">5.5.8.4</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>